Dominik created KAFKA-16222:
-------------------------------

             Summary: Incorrect default user-principal quota after migration
                 Key: KAFKA-16222
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16222
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: kraft, migration
    Affects Versions: 3.6.1
            Reporter: Dominik


We observed that our default user quota seems not to be migrated correctly.


Before Migration:

bin/kafka-configs.sh --describe --all --entity-type users

Quota configs for the *default user-principal* are consumer_byte_rate=1000000.0, producer_byte_rate=1000000.0
Quota configs for user-principal 'myuser' are consumer_byte_rate=1.5E8, producer_byte_rate=1.5E8


After Migration:

bin/kafka-configs.sh --describe --all --entity-type users

Quota configs for *user-principal ''* are consumer_byte_rate=1000000.0, producer_byte_rate=1000000.0
Quota configs for user-principal 'myuser' are consumer_byte_rate=1.5E8, producer_byte_rate=1.5E8



