>            Priority: Critical
>             Fix For: 3.7.0
>
>
> https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-14831 fixed a producer bug ab=
out internal TX state transition and the producer is now throwing an Illega=
lStateException in situations it did swallow an internal error before.
> This change surfaces a bug in Kafka Streams: Kafka Streams calls `abortTr=
ansaction()` blindly when a task is closed dirty, even if the Producer is a=
lready in an internal fatal state. However, if the Producer is in a fatal s=
tate, Kafka Streams should skip `abortTransaction` and only `close()` the P=
roducer when closing a task dirty.
> The bug is surfaced after `commitTransaction()` did timeout or after an `=
InvalidProducerEpochException` from a `send()` call, leading to the call to=
 `abortTransaction()` =E2=80=93 Kafka Streams does not track right now if a=
 commit-TX is in progress.
> {code:java}
> java.lang.IllegalStateException: Cannot attempt operation `abortTransacti=
on` because the previous call to `commitTransaction` timed out and must be =
retried
