> If the Producer throws an IllegalStateException on `abortTransaction()` K=
afka Streams treats this exception ("correctly") as fatal, and StreamsThrea=
d dies. However, Kafka Streams is actually in a state in which it can recov=
er from, and thus should not let StreamThread die by carry forward (by not =
calling `abortTransaction()` and moving forward with the dirty close of the=
 task).
> =C2=A0
