Jorge Esteban Quilcate Otoya created KAFKA-16264:
----------------------------------------------------

             Summary: Expose `producer.id.expiration.check.interval.ms` as =
dynamic broker configuration
                 Key: KAFKA-16264
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16264
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Jorge Esteban Quilcate Otoya
            Assignee: Jorge Esteban Quilcate Otoya


Dealing with a scenario where too many producer ids lead to issues (e.g. hi=
gh cpu utilization, see KAFKA-16229) put operators in need to flush produce=
r ids more promptly than usual.

Currently, only the expiration timeout `producer.id.expiration.ms` is expos=
ed as dynamic config. This is helpful (e.g. by reducing the timeout, less p=
roducer would eventually be kept in memory), but not enough if the evaluati=
on frequency is not sufficiently short to flush producer ids before becomin=
g an issue. Only by tuning both, the issue could be workaround.

=C2=A0



