Kirk True resolved KAFKA-16200.
-------------------------------
    Resolution: Duplicate

> Enforce that RequestManager implementations respect user-provided timeout
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-16200
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16200
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>          Components: clients, consumer
>            Reporter: Kirk True
>            Assignee: Kirk True
>            Priority: Blocker
>              Labels: consumer-threading-refactor, timeout
>             Fix For: 3.8.0
>
>
> The intention of the {{CompletableApplicationEvent}} is for a {{Consumer}} to block waiting for the event to complete. The application thread will block for the timeout, but there is not yet a consistent manner in which events are timed out.
> Enforce at the request manager layer that timeouts are respected per the design in KAFKA-15848.



--
