In documentation from version 3.1 to version 3.4, it looks like the retries=
 explanation has a bug related to=C2=A0max.in.flight.request.per.connection=
 related parameter and possible message reordering.

[https://kafka.apache.org/31/documentation.html#producerconfigs_retries]

[https://kafka.apache.org/32/documentation.html#producerconfigs_retries]

[https://kafka.apache.org/33/documentation.html#producerconfigs_retries]

[https://kafka.apache.org/34/documentation.html#producerconfigs_retries]

=C2=A0

in particular, the section


Allowing retries while setting=C2=A0enable.idempotence=C2=A0to=C2=A0false=
=C2=A0and=C2=A0max.in.flight.requests.per.connection=C2=A0to 1 will potenti=
ally change the ordering of records because if two batches are sent to a si=
ngle partition, and the first fails and is retried but the second succeeds,=
 then the records in the second batch may appear first.

=C2=A0

Is states=C2=A0

max.in.flight.requests.per.connection=C2=A0to 1

=C2=A0

It should be said

max.in.flight.requests.per.connection=C2=A0to=C2=A0*greater than*=C2=A0=C2=
=A01

=C2=A0

This bug has been fixed in the latest versions, but it still confuses users=
 using affected versions as the meaning is the opposite of what it should b=
e.

=C2=A0

I created a PR=C2=A0 ([https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/15413)] for ver=
sion 3.2, but the build failed. Not sure why.

=C2=A0



