Subject: Shortened URLs for KIPs?
Message-Id: <1615FC4D-8FC8-4ACC-B5F5-B7B139643B32@kirktrue.pro>
Date: Wed, 28 Feb 2024 14:40:30 -0800
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
X-Mailer: Apple Mail (2.3774.400.31)

--Apple-Mail=_33202AEE-96D1-4707-AEE2-B6FEE1EC1F60
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
Content-Type: text/plain;
	charset=utf-8

Hi all,

Is it possible to set up shortened URLs for KIPs? So instead of, say:

=
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-966%3A+Eligible+Lead=
er+Replicas

We could refer to it as:

https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-966

Or maybe even go so far as to have something like:

https://kafka.apache.org/kips/KIP-966

I know the wiki has a way to generate a short URL (e.g. =
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/mpOzDw), but, IMO, it=E2=80=99s so =
opaque as to be nearly worthless.=20

Pros:

1. Succinct: great for written documentation
2. Discoverability: it=E2=80=99s predictable and easy to find
3. Robust: the URL doesn=E2=80=99t break when the KIP title changes

Cons:

1. Time
2. Money
3. Perpetual maintenance: requires 100% commitment indefinitely

I know the list of cons is probably much more than I realize. At this =
point I=E2=80=99m just wondering if it=E2=80=99s even a desired =
mechanism.

Thoughts?

Thanks,
Kirk=

